# Require No Model Problems

This rule fails the build if Maven encountered problems while building any of the reactor's effective models.

The rule requires a Maven runtime that exposes retained model problems through either the Maven 3
`MavenSession#getModelProblems()` API or the Maven 4 session model problem collector. On Maven versions without either
capability, the rule logs a warning and is skipped. If a build must guarantee that the check is performed, constrain the
Maven runtime separately, for example with the `requireMavenVersion` rule.

The following parameter is supported by this rule:

- **message** - an optional message to use when the rule fails.

Sample Plugin Configuration:

```xml
<plugin>
  <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
  <artifactId>maven-enforcer-plugin</artifactId>
  <version>${project.version}</version>
  <executions>
    <execution>
      <id>require-clean-models</id>
      <goals>
        <goal>enforce</goal>
      </goals>
      <configuration>
        <rules>
          <requireNoModelProblems/>
        </rules>
      </configuration>
    </execution>
  </executions>
</plugin>
```
